# API Development Guidelines

## Route Structure

- Use RESTful conventions (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Group routes by resource in `/server/routes/`
- Use middleware for auth, validation, error handling

## Request Handling

- Always validate request bodies using the validation middleware
- Use pagination utility for list endpoints
- Return consistent error shapes via errorHandler middleware

## Response Format

```javascript
// Success
{ data: {...}, meta: { page, limit, total } }

// Error
{ error: { code, message, details } }
```

## Database

- Use parameterized queries (never string concatenation)
- Handle transactions for multi-step operations
- Use the db utilities in `/server/db/`

## Security

- Never expose internal errors to clients
- Validate all user inputs
- Use auth middleware on protected routes
- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens)
